            <value>The patient had Emergency Symptoms During Triage</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/treatment_severe_dehydration:label">
            <value>Severe Dehydration: Place Levine tube, provide ORS via tube, advise mother to give frequent sips of ORS and continue breastfeeding during transfer.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/confirm_treatment_severe_dehydration_levin_tube:label">
            <value>Did you place a Levine tube?</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/confirm_treatment_severe_dehydration_ORS:label">
            <value>Did you provide 1 ORS packet via Levine tube?</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/treatment_respiratory_distress:label">
            <value>Respiratory Distress: Give first dose of amoxicillin oral suspension, administer oxygen if available, keep airway clear and position child comfortably.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/confirm_treatment_respiratory_distress:label">
            <value>Did you administer the first dose of amoxicillin oral suspension?</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/treatment_altered_consciousness:label">
            <value>Altered Consciousness / Convulsions / Whimpering: Manage airway, position on side (recovery position), give diazepam if actively convulsing, treat to prevent hypoglycemia, and keep warm.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/confirm_treatment_altered_consciousness:label">
            <value>Did you give 1 diazepam?</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/treatment_acute_malnutrition:label">
            <value>Complicated Acute Malnutrition: Keep child warm to prevent hypothermia, give oral glucose/sugar water to prevent low blood sugar, do not force-feed.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/confirm_treatment_acute_malnutrition:label">
            <value>Did you give the child orgal glucose?</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/treatment_bloated_extremities:label">
            <value>Bloated Child / Inflamed Lower Limbs / Anuria: Position upright, monitor vitals closely, avoid fluid overload, and prepare for immediate specialized renal/pediatric transfer.</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/grp_triage_emergency/emergency_symptoms_during_triage_not_confirmed_reason:label">
